            <rel name="conjunction" type="multinuc"/>
        </relations>
    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="15" relname="background">I work for a large "Fortune 100" company that uses web sites for every imaginable purpose.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="20" relname="span">The problem is that most of them are so slow</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="2" relname="volitional-result">one can go get a cup of coffee between queries.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="18" relname="span">I wouldn't mind the slow queries so much</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="21" relname="span">if the pages offered status bars to let the user know that a given percentage of the process had been completed.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="19" relname="span">This would also provide feedback to the user that the click on the web page had actually implemented a function.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="6" relname="elaboration">Often I am so used to poor query times that I don't think to make sure that the click on a button or other web logistic actually caused an action.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="17" relname="elaboration">Yes, status update bars, in my opinion, are crucial to good web site design and implementation.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="22" relname="span">Another area of web page design that causes me problems is when web sites implement their own web buttons for such common things as BACK and HOME.</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="23" relname="span">Why not use the browser provided button for this instead of implementing them in a proprietary manner?</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="10" relname="elaboration">Beware the site that boldly announces for the user not to use the browser provided navigation buttons.</segment>
        <segment id="12" parent="14" relname="volitional-result">Thanks for the opportunity to vent these frustrations.</segment>
        <group id="13" type="span"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="13" relname="span"/>
        <group id="15" type="multinuc" parent="14" relname="span"/>
        <group id="16" type="span" parent="15" relname="conjunction"/>
        <group id="17" type="span" parent="16" relname="span"/>
        <group id="18" type="span" parent="17" relname="span"/>
        <group id="19" type="span" parent="5" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="20" type="span" parent="4" relname="solutionhood"/>
        <group id="21" type="span" parent="18" relname="condition"/>
        <group id="22" type="span" parent="15" relname="conjunction"/>
        <group id="23" type="span" parent="9" relname="elaboration"/>
    </body>
</rst>
